NOTES (transparency / honesty covenant):
- Surface = com/teslasync/feature-views/NotificationChannelsView: NotificationChannelsView.kt (composable),
  NotificationChannelsViewModel.kt (S8-bound state holder), NotificationChannelsViewProjection.kt (pure model),
  NotificationChannelsViewSource.kt (S7/S8 data seam). Package io.teslasync.android.featureviews.notificationchannelsview.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton chrome), empty (EmptyState), error (ErrorDisplay + retry), stale/offline
  (DataFreshness chip + auto-refresh), content. Toasts (useToast) surfaced via shared ToastHost from a typed
  ChannelToast stream; all strings resolve through the existing P1/S10 catalog (translation_notifications_channels_*,
  translation_notifications_stats_*, translation_common_*). No new string resources were required.
- Web <BrowserPushChannelCard/> is intentionally NOT ported: it registers a browser Web-Push subscription
  (service worker + Notification API), a capability with no native Android-Compose analogue (Android push is FCM,
  a separate subsystem). Declared here to avoid silent drift.
- Instrumented UI/a11y test authored at src/androidTest/.../notificationchannelsview/NotificationChannelsViewUiTest.kt
  (per-state render + a11y label + Add-modal coverage), using the correct member-call assertExists() style (like the
  sibling AlertsSectionUiTest). The androidTest SOURCE SET as a whole has PRE-EXISTING compile breakage in unrelated
  sibling widget tests (they wrongly import androidx.compose.ui.test.assertExists/assertDoesNotExist, which are
  member functions in Compose BOM 2026.04). This is a baseline condition unrelated to this surface; the P3 gate does
  not build androidTest (assembleRelease + testReleaseUnitTest only), so EXIT is unaffected.
- Gate task paths: the prompt template uses :app: but settings.gradle.kts maps the single module to :android: (app/);
  the equivalent :android: tasks were run.

